          "description": "Vogue grew up in New York's ballroom scene, is danced to house-like music and is performed at balls; waacking comes from Los Angeles disco clubs, is danced to disco and funk and is performed in battles. Both use posing and arm work, and the difference often shows in the wrists and the whole body language. Waack Nation sums it up: \"Vogue is about the pictures, Waacking is about the movies.\" Tyrone Proctor would stop a waacking battle if someone vogued in it.",
