          "summary": "A strike: the arm drives out from the centre of the chest with force, the chest behind it.",
          "description": "The move the style is named for — and it is a strike, not a circle. The dictionary meaning of whack is \"to strike with force\", and the old name came from the onomatopoeia of cartoons like Batman. Versa-Style teaches it from the centre of the chest: the arm whacks out to the side with power as the chest activates towards it, then the other arm. Circles are rolls, not whacks.",
